      "side": 1,
      "message": "Updated in PS6: `switch_vendor` (`type: string`, `example: juniper`) is now in the `Interface` component schema and in both the POST and PATCH `/interfaces/{hostName}` request bodies in `swagger.yaml`, since those bodies inline their schemas and adding it next to `vendor` in the component alone would not have covered create/update, and both example host JSON blocks in `docs/quads-api.md` now show the field.\n\nI also added an `interfaces.switch_vendor` row to the queryable-field table in `docs/quads-host-metadata-search.md`: slightly beyond the two files you named, but the nested filter (`?interfaces.switch_vendor\u003darista`) already resolves today, so it seemed worth documenting while the field is fresh.\n\nAccepted values are the enabled switch plugin names (`juniper`, `arista`), and a NULL value keeps the historical Juniper default for interfaces created before the field existed. Note the SwaggerHub page linked from `docs/quads-api.md` is a manual publication, so it needs a re-upload to pick this up.",
